1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,556
Teacher midterm practice, question 23.

2
00:00:04,176 --> 00:00:09,156
True or false: the valence electrons in a carbon atom can form four s p

3
00:00:09,156 --> 00:00:14,070
three hybrid orbitals, which form four directional ionic bonds.

4
00:00:15,770 --> 00:00:18,578
Check the statement one piece at a time.

5
00:00:18,578 --> 00:00:23,894
The first part is right: carbon forms four s p three hybrid orbitals, pointing to

6
00:00:23,894 --> 00:00:28,374
the corners of a tetrahedron at one hundred nine point five degrees.

7
00:00:28,994 --> 00:00:32,544
But those orbitals share electrons with their neighbors.

8
00:00:32,544 --> 00:00:36,149
Shared electrons make covalent bonds, not ionic ones.

9
00:00:36,149 --> 00:00:40,713
Ionic bonds come from electron transfer, and they are not directional.

10
00:00:42,313 --> 00:00:44,209
So the answer is B: false.

11
00:00:45,029 --> 00:00:49,718
One wrong word makes the whole statement false. Here, it is the word ionic.
